    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Conversely, if the upstream can fail, you would use [`mapError(_:)`](publisher/maperror(_:).md) to provide instructions on converting the error types to needed by the downstream publisher’s inputs.",
      "normalizedSource": "Conversely, if the upstream can fail, you would use [`mapError(_:)`](publisher/maperror(_:).md) to provide instructions on converting the error types to needed by the downstream publisher’s inputs.",
      "sourceHash": "5d8f97f212b3636c0f42cb7c341bbe39ba9559ac57d89c7a154f9423f10769f5",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Use [`setFailureType(to:)`](publisher/setfailuretype(to:).md) when you need set the error type of a publisher that cannot fail.",
      "contextAfter": "The following example has two publishers with mismatched error types: `pub1`’s error type is [`Never`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Never), and `pub2`’s error type is [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error).",
      "documentTitle": "setFailureType(to:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0012:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0012",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The following example has two publishers with mismatched error types: `pub1`’s error type is [`Never`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Never), and `pub2`’s error type is [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error).",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example has two publishers with mismatched error types: `pub1`’s error type is [`Never`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Never), and `pub2`’s error type is [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error).",
      "sourceHash": "8c2f7c3f905b4139e7b27c5eae088a8b2ffa02af12620c001d969fd90b2203df",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Conversely, if the upstream can fail, you would use [`mapError(_:)`](publisher/maperror(_:).md) to provide instructions on converting the error types to needed by the downstream publisher’s inputs.",
      "contextAfter": "Because of the mismatch, the [`combineLatest(_:)`](publisher/combinelatest(_:).md) operator requires that `pub1` use [`setFailureType(to:)`](publisher/setfailuretype(to:).md) to make it appear that `pub1` can produce the [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error) type, like `pub2` can.",
      "documentTitle": "setFailureType(to:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0012:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0012",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Because of the mismatch, the [`combineLatest(_:)`](publisher/combinelatest(_:).md) operator requires that `pub1` use [`setFailureType(to:)`](publisher/setfailuretype(to:).md) to make it appear that `pub1` can produce the [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error) type, like `pub2` can.",
      "normalizedSource": "Because of the mismatch, the [`combineLatest(_:)`](publisher/combinelatest(_:).md) operator requires that `pub1` use [`setFailureType(to:)`](publisher/setfailuretype(to:).md) to make it appear that `pub1` can produce the [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error) type, like `pub2` can.",
      "sourceHash": "fc1d87a914b373f37bd0778616faa3cef5c1ef70dd014812d5a3e360c4074861",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The following example has two publishers with mismatched error types: `pub1`’s error type is [`Never`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Never), and `pub2`’s error type is [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error).",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nlet pub1 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].publisher\nlet pub2 = CurrentValueSubject<Int, Error>(0)\nlet cancellable = pub1\n    .setFailureType(to: Error.self)\n    .combineLatest(pub2)\n    .sink(\n        receiveCompletion: { print (\"completed: \\($0)\") },\n        receiveValue: { print (\"value: \\($0)\")}\n     )\n\n// Prints: \"value: (5, 0)\".\n```",
      "documentTitle": "setFailureType(to:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0013:0001",
      "blockId": "code:discussion:0013",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nlet pub1 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].publisher\nlet pub2 = CurrentValueSubject<Int, Error>(0)\nlet cancellable = pub1\n    .setFailureType(to: Error.self)\n    .combineLatest(pub2)\n    .sink(\n        receiveCompletion: { print (\"completed: \\($0)\") },\n        receiveValue: { print (\"value: \\($0)\")}\n     )\n\n// Prints: \"value: (5, 0)\".\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift let pub1 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].publisher let pub2 = CurrentValueSubject<Int, Error>(0) let cancellable = pub1 .setFailureType(to: Error.self) .combineLatest(pub2) .sink( receiveCompletion: { print (\"completed: \\($0)\") }, receiveValue: { print (\"value: \\($0)\")} ) // Prints: \"value: (5, 0)\". ```",
      "sourceHash": "a54530c66e54627355558da1c40c87d6594aa5e3856ecc335fd8b4647b98db92",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "Because of the mismatch, the [`combineLatest(_:)`](publisher/combinelatest(_:).md) operator requires that `pub1` use [`setFailureType(to:)`](publisher/setfailuretype(to:).md) to make it appear that `pub1` can produce the [`Error`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Error) type, like `pub2` can.",
      "contextAfter": "Parameters",
      "documentTitle": "setFailureType(to:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "```swift\nlet pub1 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].publisher\nlet pub2 = CurrentValueSubject<Int, Error>(0)\nlet cancellable = pub1\n    .setFailureType(to: Error.self)\n    .combineLatest(pub2)\n    .sink(\n        receiveCompletion: { print (\"completed: \\($0)\") },\n        receiveValue: { print (\"value: \\($0)\")}\n     )\n\n// Prints: \"value: (5, 0)\".\n```",
      "status": "preserved",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": true
    },
